MEASURE __
CITY ATTORNEY’S IMPARTIAL ANALYSIS
If approved, Measure __ would authorize a one percent (1% - one cent on every dollar)
transactions and use (sales) tax within the City of Chino Hills. It is estimated that Measure __
will provide an additional $11,500,00.00 annually to the City’s general fund, which is used
mainly to fund police services, open space maintenance (including wildfire prevention services),
park and street maintenance, and community programs and events. This tax would be a “general
tax,” meaning that revenues raised from the tax would be deposited into the City’s general fund
and could be used for any lawful City purpose.
The sales tax would generally be applicable to retail sales of tangible items. Like the existing
sales tax, it would not apply to sales of certain food products for human consumption, sales of
prescription medicine, tuition, rent, or utilities. Labor and services are also generally exempt
from sales tax.
California Revenue and Taxation Code section 7285.9 authorizes the City to levy a general
transactions and use (sales) tax so long as the tax is approved by a majority of the voters voting
in an election on the issue. If approved, the tax would remain in effect until ended by Chino
Hills voters voting at a subsequent election. The City Council may also choose to suspend all or
a portion of the tax at any time in its discretion.
The current sales tax rate in Chino Hills is 7.75%, of which the state receives 6%, the City
receives 1%, and the county receives 0.75%. The proposed 1% sales tax would be in addition to
the current sales tax rate. However, all revenues raised by the proposed tax would be controlled
by the City and available for local use. Neither the state nor the county would share in the tax
revenue.
The Chino Hills City Council placed Measure __ on the ballot. It takes a simple majority of the
votes cast to pass Measure __.
A “yes” vote is a vote in favor of the 1% transactions and use (sales) tax.
A “no” vote is a vote against the 1% transactions and use (sales) tax.
